        "title": "Swarm dev-loop authenticates against the hosted harness",
        "summary": "Dev-loop pause, stop, resume, and status calls now carry the caller's JWT through a dedicated harness transport, unblocking swarm runs against the hosted harness.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Pause, stop, resume, and status endpoints for the dev loop now extract the caller's JWT and thread it into control_loop and detached-run lookups, so hosted harness requests are properly authenticated instead of being made anonymously.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "103f2631ebc56b39284d42e74e3fd80642f63ab5"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Introduced a dedicated harness_transport module and persisted a per-run harness_auth_token alongside the harness base URL, letting each running loop reconnect to its hosted harness with the right credentials.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "103f2631ebc56b39284d42e74e3fd80642f63ab5"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "1:19 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-09T08:19:46.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-09T08:19:46.000Z",
        "title": "Task completion notifications no longer fire twice",
        "summary": "The desktop interface now briefly delays task completion toasts and suppresses them when the terminal task-run loop event arrives, eliminating duplicate notifications at the end of a run.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Task completion events are held for a short dedupe window (~2.5s) and only surfaced as a toast and OS notification if no terminal task_run LoopEnded event arrives to represent the same completion.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "bbddfd9585f8d09f6f95078bf46ef91d2f8bbb6e"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added a full test suite around useTaskNotifications covering the delayed-delivery, terminal-loop suppression, and IPC posting paths to lock in the new dedupe behavior.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "bbddfd9585f8d09f6f95078bf46ef91d2f8bbb6e"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
